---
title: Entrances
description: Twenty-five named ways for a thing to arrive — nine for text, eight for pictures, eight for blocks and whole sections. They are a menu to choose from, not a set to use all at once - pick one per kind, in one place, and the whole site follows.
eyebrow: Motion
source: src/motion/entrance.css · src/js/im-motion.js
---
<h2>Use one</h2>
{{{{code "hbs"}}}}
<h1 data-im-in="line-up">Plays when it scrolls into view</h1>      <!-- needs im-motion.js -->
<h1 class="im-in im-in-line-up">Plays on load, CSS only</h1>
{{{{/code}}}}
<p>Above the fold, "scrolls into view" <em>is</em> on load — so <code>data-im-in</code> is the one to reach for. With no JavaScript nothing is ever hidden; under <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code> nothing is hidden and nothing moves.</p>

<h2>Choose once, for the whole site</h2>
<p>Three aliases play whatever a variable names. Templates say <em>what kind of thing</em> is arriving; one line of CSS — or a theme setting — says <em>how</em>.</p>
{{{{code "hbs"}}}}
<h2 data-im-in="text">…</h2>          <!-- plays --im-in-text     (default: line-up) -->
<img data-im-in="image" …>            <!-- plays --im-in-image    (default: develop) -->
<section data-im-in="section">…</section>   <!-- --im-in-section  (default: rise)    -->
{{{{/code}}}}
{{{{code "css"}}}}
:root {
	--im-in-text: im-in-blur-in;
	--im-in-image: im-in-iris;
	--im-in-section: im-in-fade;
}
{{{{/code}}}}
<p>Any style that is a single animation can be named this way — 21 of the 25. The four that need more than that (<code>words</code>, <code>chars</code>, <code>curtain</code>, <code>frame</code>) are asked for by name.</p>

<h2>Text</h2>
<p>Press <strong>Replay</strong> on any row.</p>
{{#example code=false}}
<div class="im-cells im-cells-3" data-replay>
	<div class="im-cell" data-replay-tile><p class="im-caption" data-index="01">rise</p><p class="text-h2 font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink" data-im-in="rise" style="min-height: 2.4em">Make it easy to read.</p><span class="text-sm">The plain one: up a little, out of nothing.</span></div>
	<div class="im-cell" data-replay-tile><p class="im-caption" data-index="02">line-up</p><p class="text-h2 font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink" data-im-in="line-up" style="min-height: 2.4em">Make it easy to read.</p><span class="text-sm">Rises from behind its own baseline, as if through a slot.</span></div>
	<div class="im-cell" data-replay-tile><p class="im-caption" data-index="03">blur-in</p><p class="text-h2 font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink" data-im-in="blur-in" style="min-height: 2.4em">Make it easy to read.</p><span class="text-sm">Comes into focus.</span></div>
	<div class="im-cell" data-replay-tile><p class="im-caption" data-index="04">track-in</p><p class="text-h2 font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink" data-im-in="track-in" style="min-height: 2.4em">Make it easy to read.</p><span class="text-sm">Letters close up from wide to set.</span></div>
	<div class="im-cell" data-replay-tile><p class="im-caption" data-index="05">type</p><p class="text-h2 font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink" data-im-in="type" style="min-height: 2.4em">Make it easy to read.</p><span class="text-sm">Wiped on in steps, like a line being typed.</span></div>
	<div class="im-cell" data-replay-tile><p class="im-caption" data-index="06">words</p><p class="text-h2 font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink" data-im-in="words" style="min-height: 2.4em">Make it easy to read.</p><span class="text-sm">Word by word, each tipping upright. Needs the script.</span></div>
	<div class="im-cell" data-replay-tile><p class="im-caption" data-index="07">chars</p><p class="text-h2 font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink" data-im-in="chars" style="min-height: 2.4em">Make it easy to read.</p><span class="text-sm">Letter by letter, each popping in. Needs the script.</span></div>
	<div class="im-cell" data-replay-tile><p class="im-caption" data-index="08">flip</p><p class="text-h2 font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink" data-im-in="flip" style="min-height: 2.4em">Make it easy to read.</p><span class="text-sm">Tips up from lying flat on the page.</span></div>
	<div class="im-cell" data-replay-tile><p class="im-caption" data-index="09">pixel</p><p class="text-h2 font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink" data-im-in="pixel" style="min-height: 2.4em">Make it easy to read.</p><span class="text-sm">Arrives in Geist Pixel, then resolves into its own face. The system's signature.</span></div>
</div>
{{/example}}

<h2>Image</h2>
{{#example code=false}}
<div class="im-cells im-cells-4" data-replay>
	<div class="im-cell" data-replay-tile><p class="im-caption" data-index="10">wipe-right</p><figure class="im-fx-img" style="aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; overflow: hidden"><img data-im-in="wipe-right" src="{{demo.three.[0].feature_image}}" alt="" loading="lazy"></figure><span class="text-sm">Uncovered by a straight edge, left to right.</span></div>
	<div class="im-cell" data-replay-tile><p class="im-caption" data-index="11">wipe-up</p><figure class="im-fx-img" style="aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; overflow: hidden"><img data-im-in="wipe-up" src="{{demo.three.[0].feature_image}}" alt="" loading="lazy"></figure><span class="text-sm">Uncovered from the bottom.</span></div>
	<div class="im-cell" data-replay-tile><p class="im-caption" data-index="12">iris</p><figure class="im-fx-img" style="aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; overflow: hidden"><img data-im-in="iris" src="{{demo.three.[0].feature_image}}" alt="" loading="lazy"></figure><span class="text-sm">Opens from the centre, like a lens.</span></div>
	<div class="im-cell" data-replay-tile><p class="im-caption" data-index="13">blinds</p><figure class="im-fx-img" style="aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; overflow: hidden"><img data-im-in="blinds" src="{{demo.three.[0].feature_image}}" alt="" loading="lazy"></figure><span class="text-sm">Eight slats open together.</span></div>
	<div class="im-cell" data-replay-tile><p class="im-caption" data-index="14">zoom-out</p><figure class="im-fx-img" style="aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; overflow: hidden"><img data-im-in="zoom-out" src="{{demo.three.[0].feature_image}}" alt="" loading="lazy"></figure><span class="text-sm">Settles back from slightly too close.</span></div>
	<div class="im-cell" data-replay-tile><p class="im-caption" data-index="15">develop</p><figure class="im-fx-img" style="aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; overflow: hidden"><img data-im-in="develop" src="{{demo.three.[0].feature_image}}" alt="" loading="lazy"></figure><span class="text-sm">Like a print in the tray: pale and soft, then colour and edge.</span></div>
	<div class="im-cell" data-replay-tile><p class="im-caption" data-index="16">curtain</p><figure class="im-fx-img" data-im-in="curtain" style="aspect-ratio: 4 / 3"><img src="{{demo.three.[0].feature_image}}" alt="" loading="lazy"></figure><span class="text-sm">A panel of the accent crosses and leaves the picture behind it. On the wrapper.</span></div>
	<div class="im-cell" data-replay-tile><p class="im-caption" data-index="17">tilt</p><figure class="im-fx-img" style="aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; overflow: hidden"><img data-im-in="tilt" src="{{demo.three.[0].feature_image}}" alt="" loading="lazy"></figure><span class="text-sm">Swings in on a vertical hinge.</span></div>
</div>
{{/example}}
<p>The clipping styles (<code>wipe</code>, <code>iris</code>, <code>blinds</code>, <code>unfold</code>) hide nothing from a search engine or a screen reader — the picture is in the page from the first byte; only its paint is delayed.</p>

